David Jao wrote:
>
> If I make it to the castle, I always spend one of the wishes on an "AoLS.
> Expert players can no doubt make better use of both the equipment slot and
> the wish, but IMO until you become an expert, don't worry too much about
> optimizing for the expert player case.

The range between novice and expert is very much
floating point not binary.  Each lesson learned leads
to doing something different in future games.
Perhaps it's learning which monsters are not poisonous
but can convey poison resistance, perhaps it's hoarding
all wnads of death to make quick work of returning
Rodneys.  There could be thousands of such small
modifications of your strategy between having trouble
surviving long enough to know that the mines are a
separate branch through increasing your ascension
percentage.

> It doesn't protect you against every single possible stupid action, but it
> protects against enough of them to be worth it.

And as usual in Nethack it comes with a cost.  "oR is one
of the few sources of reflection and reflection is very
important for survival as you get deeper.  What other
important factor are you willing to drop to switch
amulets?  Drop twoweapon for a shield and drop spell
casting?  Drop GDSM for SDSM and get MR some other way?
And as usual in Nethack there are many right answers and
infinite wrong answers.



